# COD Bloom on D3D11 (0) or the render graph (1): Whiterun at 13:00 in clear weather, then Dragonsreach, a shot of each.
# Sub-effects this test expects, under "PostProcessing" in SettingsUser.json:
#   "COD Bloom": { "enabled": true }   (Composite turns itself on with it and reads the bloom: it needs its own ORG port)
#   "Depth of Field", "Local Exposure", "Histogram Auto Exposure", "Lens Flare", "Motion Blur", "Physical Glare",
#   "Camera", "Vignette", "Color Grading and Tone Mapping", "LUT", "Border": { "enabled": false }
#   (Vignette, Color Grading, LUT and Border may stay on: they are ported.)
#   A strong bloom makes a difference easy to see: "COD Bloom": { "settings": { "Threshold": -2.0, "BlendFactor": 0.3 } }.
# Effects11 must not own the tonemap (its effect off), or Post Processing does not run at all.
# With 1, the log shows "[ORG] Post Processing: chain built (input, cod-bloom, composite, output; ...)" and "the chain runs
# on the render graph". Without Composite's port it shows "the chain runs on D3D11: Composite has no ORG implementation"
# and nothing names COD Bloom. Compare the shots with the 0 run: the glow around bright sky and fires should match.
CS_ORG_POST_PROCESSING=1
DXVK_DEBUG=hang
VK_LOADER_LAYERS_DISABLE=*nsight*
CS_DCLF_TEST_COMMANDS=600:set timescale to 0;601:set gamehour to 13;602:fw 81a;700:coc Whiterun;2000:fw 81a;2400:dclf:shot=whiterun;2500:coc WhiterunDragonsreach;3600:dclf:shot=dragonsreach
CS_DCLF_TEST_EXIT=3700
